    "created_at": "2026-09-22T16:09:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-22T16:09:10Z",
    "body": "@annevk The place where this seemed to be a problem was for [createPattern](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-context-2d-createpattern), where its not clear what to do with a non-existing width & height, so if \"[check the usability of the image argument](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#check-the-usability-of-the-image-argument)\" really did mean to return bad when they didn't exist it would be helpful. \n\nI did a bit of digging, and it turns out I forgot I filed an issue on this a few years ago - https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10495.\n\nBut I think you are right, and check usability really does mean to return good for non-existing width & height. So maybe changing the language to:\n\n> \"If image has a [natural width](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-width) or [natural height](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-height) (or both) that exist and are equal to zero, then return bad.\n\nIt's a bit redundant, but I think worth it for a bit more clarity.",
